@@ -88,3 +88,32 @@ Paths are absolute and contain no `..` component. The key file is mode `0600`, o
 ## What darkapi sees
 
 Signals are `darksignal.signal.v2`: the v1 fields plus `priority`, and for store alerts `subject_host` (the host the alert is about) and `source_ref`. The heartbeat is v2 and carries ingest counters (`accepted`, `dropped`, `rejected`, `evicted`, `ack_errors`, `store_errors`), `last_frame_ms`, and `problem` when a route is missing. TLS is 1.3 only. See [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md).
+
+
+## Darkapple (macOS)
+
+The host-mode producer `darkapple` accepts versioned `darkapple.event.v1`
+records from the configured Rust daemon executable/uid. Configure it as:
+
+```json
+"darkapple": {"exe": "/Applications/Darkapple.app/Contents/MacOS/darkappled", "uid": 0}
+```
+
+Use the same configured host and a shared local socket. The classifier maps
+macOS hidden/temporary executables, launchd changes, SIP/Gatekeeper posture,
+and sensor loss/coverage rules. Unknown Darkapple rules are refused rather
+than acknowledged and discarded. Signals carry a `darkapple.event` source
+reference and include the durable event ID in deduplication. The static ship
+route is `/v1/darksignal/darkapple`; its backend receiver must be provisioned
+separately before claiming fleet delivery.
+
+Authenticated `darkapple.health.v1` frames update producer health without
+creating threat signals. The Darksignal heartbeat includes `darkapple` with
+`last_health_ms` and status `unseen`, `available`, `degraded`, or `silent`
+(after 90 seconds or a backward receiver clock). Unseen does not mean that
+Darkapple is configured on every host. Backend alerting on this field remains
+an API responsibility. Runtime health is reset when Darksignal restarts.
+
+Darkapple retains refused records because ACK 0 includes temporary capacity
+and storage failures. ACK 1 remains local handling, not remote delivery.
+See the sibling `darkapple/docs/protocol.md` for the body and rule contract.
